Z||000005||martin1875||11-29-2000||11:06 PM||||i have never changed a rear seal on a fiero,i just got my first one and i am having starting problems.i have been doing mechanic work for a long time and have had the rear seal problem before on a lot of different engine types.as for your car i would check a manuel, i have seen lots of differet seals , some seals are made into the rear main-bearing cap. some you have to pull the flywheel to change.i am not sure of the engine you have so again check a manuel for correct way||||reg||1
Z||000006||varnster||11-29-2000||11:29 PM||||Thanks for your help but I got it licked, its<BR>the distibuter man! Im still jumping up and down with a stupid smile on my face! I checked the holy archives and dude had the<BR>same prob He changed the pan gasket to, the<BR>prob is a 90 cent o ring found at NAPA. I<BR>guess this is a comman prob that the o ring<BR>dryrots and drip drip drip. thanks again and<BR>enjoy the hell out of that new rod!||||reg||1
Z||000007||StuGood||11-30-2000||08:35 AM||||That's one of the things I like best about Fieros... they sometimes display fairly scary-looking / annoying symptoms, which often are caused by problems with really simple, low-cost solutions! Makes used-Fiero shopping a bargain hunt... makes Fiero repair a rewarding experience  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">!<P>Whenever there's a leak towards the "back" (LHS) of the engine, distributor o-ring is the 1st thing I check.  I don't know if the oil gets "slung" by something or what, but when that thing leaks, it can get all over everywhere.  Makes it look like a rear main leak, transaxle leak, etc.  But the o-ring is almost always worth a try- it's cheap and easy to do.||||reg||14
Z||000008||Fiero_Freak||11-30-2000||03:50 PM||||I sure wish I would have read this before..  Same here... except I went through the oil pan gasket, and all the way down through the intake and valve covers.  Lots of work... but I did get to lash the valves.  Now they're set, but make more noise than they ever did before?   Does anyone think I should worry about that?<BR>||||reg||9
